Article 3 (Formulation of Research Plans)
(1) The President of the Audit and Inspection Research Institute (hereinafter referred to as the "President of the Institute") shall formulate a research plan for the following year and report it to the Chairperson of the Board of Audit and Inspection (hereinafter referred to as the "Chairperson") by the end of each year. <Amended on January 5, 2009.>
(2) The research plan under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters: <Amended on January 5, 2009; and July 15, 2019.>
1. Investigation and research to develop and support audit and inspection matters of the Secretariat of the Board of Audit and Inspection;
2. Investigation and research to develop auditing and inspection methods and analytical techniques;
3. Investigation and research on changes in the audit and inspection environment over the short and long term;
4. Research on domestic and foreign audit and inspection systems and on establishing audit and inspection infrastructure;
5. Other necessary matters.
